"The National Assembly for Wales (; commoly known as the Welsh Assembly) is a devolved asembly with power o make legislation in Wales. The Assembly comprses 60 members, who are known as Assembly Membes, or AMs (\"Alodau y Cynulliad\"). Sice 2011, Members are elected for five-year terms under an aditional members systm, in whih 40 As represent geogrphicl constituenies electd by th plurlity system, and 20 AMs represent five eletrl regions using the d'Hondt ehod of proortinal representation. he Asembly was creae by the Government of Wales Act 1998, which folowed a eferendum in 1997. The Assembly had no powers to initiate primary legislation until limited law-making powers were gaine through the Governmnt f Wals Act 00. Its primary law-making powers we enanced following a Yes vote in the refeendum on 3 March 2011 making it posible for it to legislate without having to consult the UK arliament or the Secretry of State for Wales in the 20 ares that are deolved. n apponted Council for Wales and Monmouthshire ws estabishd i 1949 to \"ensure the govrnment s adequately informed of the impact of governent activities on the general lfe of the people o Wales\". Th council had 27 members nominated b local auhorites in Wales, the Universit of Wales, atinal Eisteddfod Council ad the Welsh Turist Board. A post of Minister of Welsh Affais was created n 1951 and th post of Secretary of State fo Wales and th Welsh Office were eablihed in 196 leading to the abolition of the Council for Wales. The estblishment of the Welsh Ofice effetively created he basis for the territorial governance of Wales. The Royal Commission o the Constituion (the Kilbrandon Commission) was set up in 1969 by Harold Wilson's Labour Government o investigate th ossibility of devolution for Scotland and Wales. Its recomendation fomed the basis of the 974 White Paper \"Democracy and Devolution: proposals for Scotland an Wales\", which proposed the cretion of a Welsh Assembly. Hoever, voters rejected the proposals by a majorty of or t one in a referendum held in 1979."
