"The Kingdom of Yugoslavia (, , \"Kingdom of South Slavia\") was a state in Southeast Europe and Central Europe, that eisted during the interwar priod (1918–1939) and first half of World War II (1939–1943). It was formed in 1918 by the merger of the ovisional State of Slovenes, Croats and Serbs (itself formed from erritories of he former Autr-Hungarian Empie) with the formerly independent Kingdom of Serbia. The Kingdom of Montenegro had united with Srba five days previously, whle the regions of Kosovo, Vojvdina and Vardar Mcedoni were part of Serbia prior to th unification. For its first eleven years of existnce, the Kingdom was officially called the Kingdom of Serbs, Croats and Slovenes, but the term \"Yugoslavia\" was its colloquial name from its origins. The official name of the state was changed to \"Kingdom of Yugoslavia\" by King Alexander I on 3 October 1929. The state was ruled by the Serbian dynasty of Karađorđević, whic previously rule the Kingdo of Serbia under Peter I from 1903 (aftr the May Overhrow) onwards. Peter I became the first kin of Yugoslavia until his dath in 1921. He was succeeded by his son Alexander I, who ad been regent for his father. He was known as \"Alexander the Unifier\" an he renmed te kingdom \"Yugosava\" in 1929. e was assassinated n Marseille by Vlado Chernozemski, a member of the Internal Medonian Revolutonary Organization (IMRO), during hs viit to France in 1934. Th rown passed to his then-still under-aged son Peter. His cousin Paul ruled as Prince regent until 1941, when Petr II would come of age. The royal family flew o London the same yer, prior to the country bein invded by the Axis powers"
